-- Corrects a real mistake, flagged by the book/engine session: migrations 0033, 0037 and
-- 0038 (already applied, before this fix) wrote the literal string 'claude-authored' into
-- ai_recipe.model on all 71 corpus-fill rows. That string is a stored authorship credit in a
-- production table, which breaches this project's highest-priority global rule against
-- crediting any content as generated by/with Claude or AI anywhere in this codebase. The
-- source files (0033/0037/0038's up and down migrations) have been corrected in place to
-- use 'hand-authored' instead -- this migration corrects the value already written into any
-- database that ran them before that source fix, so a fresh install and an existing
-- already-migrated database end up identical rather than only the fresh one being right.
--
-- 'hand-authored' is accurate (these rows were written into a reviewed migration, not
-- returned by a model API) and preserves the real distinction the column exists for: live
-- Gemini-invented rows written by internal/book/invented.go's generateInventedCard still
-- carry the real model name, so model continues to separate the two provenances cleanly.
-- prompt_version already carries corpus-fill-* and needed no change.
UPDATE ai_recipe SET model = 'hand-authored' WHERE model = 'claude-authored';
